#
# A coverage-guided campaign writes into this directory as it runs. Without
# these rules a one-hour `run-all.sh` leaves thousands of untracked files in
# `git status`, which is how a real finding gets lost in the noise — and how
# a repo-wide auto-commit sweeps machine-specific bytes into history.

# cargo-fuzz's build output.
target/
Cargo.lock.fuzz

# `corpus/gen_seeds.py` is importable, so anything that imports it (a
# validation script, a REPL) leaves bytecode next to the seeds.
__pycache__/

# Crash artifacts and per-target logs are per-run and machine-specific.
# A *reproducer worth keeping* is committed deliberately:
#     git add -f fuzz/artifacts/<target>/crash-<sha1>
# `replay-corpus.sh` then replays it on every commit, so the fix stays fixed.
artifacts/

# Corpus entries libFuzzer discovers during a campaign. They are genuinely
# useful — but they arrive by the thousand with SHA1-hex names, and which
# ones are worth keeping is a `cargo fuzz cmin` decision, not a default.
#
# Two prefixes stay tracked: `seed-*` (everything `corpus/gen_seeds.py`
# writes) and `regression-*` (a minimized crash input committed after the
# bug it found was fixed — see "Crash Triage" in README.md).
corpus/*/*
!corpus/*/seed-*
!corpus/*/regression-*
